{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "cues": [
    {
      "id": "craft-escape-v2-cue-1",
      "transcript": "To escape slavery, Ellen Craft posed as a white male slaveholder. Her husband William posed as her enslaved servant.",
      "file": "audio/craft-escape-v2/narration/cue-1.wav",
      "start": 0,
      "duration": 8.325,
      "beatIndex": 0,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "craft-escape.asset.open-escape.script.1",
      "samples": 199800,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "craft-escape-v2-cue-2",
      "transcript": "In 1848, they traveled openly by train and steamer. But Ellen could not write. What if she had to sign?",
      "file": "audio/craft-escape-v2/narration/cue-2.wav",
      "start": 8.466666666666667,
      "duration": 7.325,
      "beatIndex": 1,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "craft-escape.asset.open-escape.script.2",
      "samples": 175800,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "craft-escape-v2-cue-3",
      "transcript": "She bound her right hand to make it appear injured—an excuse not to sign, reported weeks after their escape.",
      "file": "audio/craft-escape-v2/narration/cue-3.wav",
      "start": 16.033333333333335,
      "duration": 7.125,
      "beatIndex": 2,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "craft-escape.asset.open-escape.script.3",
      "samples": 171000,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "craft-escape-v2-cue-4",
      "transcript": "Their later book describes more: bandages hid her beardless chin, spectacles obscured her face, and apparent illness excused conversation.",
      "file": "audio/craft-escape-v2/narration/cue-4.wav",
      "start": 23.3,
      "duration": 9.375,
      "beatIndex": 3,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "craft-escape.asset.open-escape.script.4",
      "samples": 225000,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "craft-escape-v2-cue-5",
      "transcript": "William sustained the disguise as her attendant.",
      "file": "audio/craft-escape-v2/narration/cue-5.wav",
      "start": 32.833333333333336,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "beatIndex": 4,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "craft-escape.asset.open-escape.script.5",
      "samples": 80400,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "craft-escape-v2-cue-6",
      "transcript": "But disguise could not answer every question. In Baltimore, their account says officials demanded assurance that the supposed master had the right to take William onward.",
      "file": "audio/craft-escape-v2/narration/cue-6.wav",
      "start": 36.333333333333336,
      "duration": 10.925,
      "beatIndex": 5,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "craft-escape.asset.open-escape.script.6",
      "samples": 262200,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "craft-escape-v2-cue-7",
      "transcript": "Appearance was not proof of ownership.",
      "file": "audio/craft-escape-v2/narration/cue-7.wav",
      "start": 47.4,
      "duration": 2.575,
      "beatIndex": 6,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "craft-escape.asset.open-escape.script.7",
      "samples": 61800,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "craft-escape-v2-cue-8",
      "transcript": "William’s account says a conductor confirmed their earlier train journey. As departure approached, the officer let them through, citing the apparent master’s illness.",
      "file": "audio/craft-escape-v2/narration/cue-8.wav",
      "start": 50.233333333333334,
      "duration": 10.4,
      "beatIndex": 7,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "craft-escape.asset.open-escape.script.8",
      "samples": 249600,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "craft-escape-v2-cue-9",
      "transcript": "After four days, they reached Philadelphia. Reaching the North did not guarantee safety. In 1850, men came to Boston to recapture them. The Crafts left for England.",
      "file": "audio/craft-escape-v2/narration/cue-9.wav",
      "start": 60.766666666666666,
      "duration": 11.625,
      "beatIndex": 8,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "craft-escape.asset.open-escape.script.9",
      "samples": 279000,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "craft-escape-v2-cue-10",
      "transcript": "Their ingenuity turned a system’s assumptions against it. Treated as property, they escaped together by making it appear that one owned the other.",
      "file": "audio/craft-escape-v2/narration/cue-10.wav",
      "start": 72.63333333333334,
      "duration": 8.8,
      "beatIndex": 9,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "craft-escape.asset.open-escape.script.10",
      "samples": 211200,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    }
  ],
